config KDLOCK_REBUILD
	bool "kdlock private mutex core for source rebuild"
	depends on X86_64 && !PREEMPT_RT
	select EXECMEM
	help
	  Package the source-rebuilt ordinary mutex core, task-owned storage,
	  immutable-text provider, executable image loader and bounded compiler
	  control channel. The exact Linux 7.0 task fields and lifecycle hooks
	  must already be integrated. Resource counts and complete auxiliary
	  control-stack bounds are explicit provider inputs, without defaults.

	  All admitted source dependencies must remain immutable through their
	  actual native, generated and feedback users. This option supplies no
	  automatic Linux mutex aliases or additional API/context lane, and
	  enabling it establishes no build, execution or performance evidence.
	  See kernel/integration/BUILDING.md in the kdlock package.
